# Strike Up the Score: Deriving Searchable and Playable Digital Formats from Sheet Music; Smart Objects and Open Archives; Building the Archives of the Future: Advanced in Preserving Electronic Records at the National Archives and Records Administration; From the Digitized to the Digital Library.

**Authors:** Choudhury, G. Sayeed, DiLauro, Tim, Droettboom, Michael, Fujinaga, Ichiro, MacMillan, Karl, Nelson, Michael L., Maly, Kurt, Thibodeau, Kenneth, Thaller, Manfred

## Abstract
These articles describe the experiences of the Johns Hopkins University library in digitizing their collection of sheet music; motivation for buckets, Smart Object, Dumb Archive (SODA) and the Open Archives Initiative (OAI), and initial experiences using them in digital library (DL) testbeds; requirements for archival institutions, the National Archives and Records Administration (NARA) preserving information in digital form; digital libraries and the systematic conversion of library resources into digital form. (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ626728

